// What makes a build the whole app for other people: the normal app, reading the hosted server, with its own settings, records, sandbox and
// Keychain group, so it can never see the normal build's wallet. Only macos/hosted.sh uses this, with xcodebuild's -xcconfig, so every target
// and package sees it and `pnpm mac` never does. What it signs with is in Hosted.entitlements.

SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) PATINA_HOSTED

// The last word of each names its socket, so neither can be the normal build's `wallet` or `debug`.
APP_BUNDLE_ID = com.benface.pricetag.macos.hosted
APP_DEBUG_BUNDLE_ID = com.benface.pricetag.macos.hosteddebug

// The hosted server, from App.xcconfig. macos/hosted.sh sets this over it for --local, which reads this Mac's server and is never notarized.
PATINA_SERVER_HOST = $(PATINA_HOSTED_SERVER_HOST)
